From 81f0e38d16ba58a9f7f43427073e860091f61d55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ashforde=20O=C3=9C?= <ashfordegithub@cbaweja.org>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:12:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(desktop): live devices (L2b): the trust page scores a
 receiver live in Kshana Desktop

The app reads a receiver's NMEA 0183 output read only, from a serial or
USB port, a TCP stream (tcp:<host>:<port>) or a growing file (file:<path>),
and keeps the latest 1.5 MiB of sentences. The trust page's new panel,
shown only in the Desktop, scores that excerpt with the native engine
every five seconds and draws it in the view.

- apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/devices.rs: port listing (Linux by-id and
  tty names, macOS cu.*, Windows SERIALCOMM), capture thread, rolling
  excerpt, status, stop; serial speed set with stty when chosen.
- bridge.rs: receiver_trust_replay and assess_vessel_log run natively.
- web/studio/lib/devices.mjs: the command client, the native engine for
  the page and the re-score loop (no overlap, unchanged excerpts skipped).
- Tests: devices.rs (ring, sources, file and TCP capture), the native
  scorer against the engine on the demo log, devices.test.mjs (CI step).
- README, SURFACES row and the English catalogue entries.
